# Subagent models (human 2026-08-16)

Parent is **usually Composer slow**. This pool is not a hard lane (not “Grok always designs, Luna always reviews”).

| Model | Task `model` slug | Best at |
|-------|-------------------|---------|
| **Composer slow** | `composer-2.5` | Default parent / build — routes, tests, docs, UI from a decision |
| **Cursor Grok 4.6 medium** | `inherit` if parent is already Grok 4.6; never Grok 4.5 | Why / design / root-cause / temporal-logic / competing approaches |
| **GPT-4.6 Luna high** | `gpt-5.6-luna-high` | AC match, honesty/empty, contract, line-by-line “did we ship the ask” |

**Review (not a hard set):** first pass = whoever is better at *this* question. **Final pass = the other one.** If Grok did design or first review, Luna is final. If Luna did first review, Grok is final. Do not skip the complementary final on hydration, contract, grading, or honesty diffs. Skip both extras on a one-liner.

**Do not use Claude Sonnet 4.5 or Sonnet 4.6** (any thinking effort, fast/slow, or leftover “Sonnet gate”). Do not pick `claude-sonnet-*` 4.x slugs.

Also do not use unless the human explicitly asks: `composer-2.5-fast`, Grok 4.5 (`cursor-grok-4.5-*`), Grok 4.6 high-fast, Opus, Gemini, Sol, Fable, Sonnet 5.

If a Task catalog has no Grok 4.6 **medium** slug, inherit from a Grok 4.6 parent rather than substituting Sonnet or Grok 4.5. Bump Grok to high only when medium is stuck.

